# `core/testing/check`, failing, with the counterexample it names recorded.
#
# A property tester is only worth having if the failure is reproducible, so
# this case is the one that says it is. The first seed is fixed and there is no
# shrinking, so the run draws the same hundred cases every time and stops at the
# same one — and the `seed` in the report, handed to `random.seeded`, draws that
# `case` back. A change that moves the draw order moves these numbers, and a
# change that makes them wander does not compile a golden at all.
#
# The report comes out of `assert.none`, because that is how `check` reports:
# it hands the runner an `Option<Counterexample<T>>` and the runner renders it
# structurally, the way it renders both sides of every other assertion. There is
# no second reporting intrinsic — see design/native/DECISIONS.md.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs. Textproto,
# but not a Buri file: only repo/ below is a Buri repository.

doc: "core/testing/check failing, with the seed and the case its report names"

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/props", "--force", "--output=js"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "fail.txt"
  stream: OUT
}
